diff --git a/README.rst b/README.rst
index 06c8448..8784f4a 100644
--- a/README.rst
+++ b/README.rst
@@ -252,6 +252,34 @@ To use the extensions below you must import from `jsonpath_ng.ext`.
 |              | - ``$.objects[*].cow + $.objects[*].cat``        |
 +--------------+--------------------------------------------------+
 
+RFC 9535 JSONPath
+-----------------
+
+``jsonpath_ng.rfc9535`` is a strict implementation of `RFC 9535
+<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9535>`__, separate from the dialect above:
+
+.. code:: python
+
+    >>> from jsonpath_ng.rfc9535 import parse, normalized_path
+    >>> matches = parse("$.a[?@ > 1]").find({"a": [1, 2, 3]})
+    >>> [(normalized_path(m), m.value) for m in matches]
+    [("$['a'][1]", 2), ("$['a'][2]", 3)]
+
+Invalid or ill-typed queries raise ``JsonPathParserError``. The standard
+functions ``length``, ``count``, ``match``, ``search`` and ``value`` are built
+in; more can be passed to ``parse`` as ``FunctionExtension`` objects:
+
+.. code:: python
+
+    >>> from jsonpath_ng.rfc9535 import FunctionExtension, ValueType
+    >>> upper = FunctionExtension(lambda v: v.upper() if isinstance(v, str) else v,
+    ...                           (ValueType,), ValueType)
+    >>> [m.value for m in parse("$[?upper(@) == 'A']", functions={"upper": upper}).find(["a", "b"])]
+    ['a']
+
+On the command line, ``jsonpath_ng --rfc9535 QUERY [FILE ...]`` prints each
+match as JSON, and ``--paths`` prefixes it with its normalized path.
+
 About arithmetic and string
 ---------------------------
 
